<title>UK: GECC adds 150 billion lire to five-year bond.</title>
<headline>GECC adds 150 billion lire to five-year bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond was increased</p>
<p>by joint lead managers BCI and Bear Stearns.</p>
<p> BORROWER   GENERAL ELECTRIC CAPITAL CORPORATION</p>
<p> AMT ** 450 BLN LIRE  COUPON     6.125     MATURITY    31.JUL.02</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  102.735   PAY DATE    31.JUL.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  1.875     REOFFER    =	   SPREAD	=</p>
<p> MOODY	AAA	 LISTING    LUX	 PAY FREQ    =</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  AAA	 DENOMS (M) 5-50	SALE LIMITS US/UK/IT</p>
<p> NEG PLG    NO	  CRS DEFLT  YES	 FORCE MAJ   YES</p>
<p> GOV LAW    NEW YORK  HOME CTRY  =	   TAX PROVS   STD</p>
<p> MGT/UND    0.625     SELL CONC  1.25	PRAECIPUUM  =</p>
<p> NOTES	ISSUED OFF MTN PROGRAMME</p>
<p>	   ** ORIGINAL 300 BLN LIRE BOND LAUNCHED JULY 2</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
